statement.paragraph:
Let $A = \{\mathbf{a}_{1}\text{,~}\mathbf{a}_{2}\text{,~}\mathbf{a}_{3}\}$ and $D = \{\mathbf{d}_{1}\text{,~}\mathbf{d}_{2}\text{,~}\mathbf{d}_{3}\}$ be bases for $V$, and let $P = \begin{bmatrix}
      \left\lbrack \mathbf{d}_{\mathbf{1}} \right\rbrack_{A} & \left\lbrack \mathbf{d}_{2} \right\rbrack_{A} & \left\lbrack \mathbf{d}_{3} \right\rbrack_{A}
      \end{bmatrix}$. Which of the following equations is satisfied by $P$ for all $\mathbf{x}$ in $V$?

(T/F) If $V = \text{ℝ}^{2}$, $B = \left\{ \mathbf{b}_{1},\mathbf{b}_{2} \right\}$, and $C = \left\{ \mathbf{c}_{1},\mathbf{c}_{2} \right\}$, then row reduction of $\begin{bmatrix}
      \text{c}_{1} & \text{c}_{\text{2}} & \mathbf{b}_{1} & \mathbf{b}_{\text{2}}
      \end{bmatrix}$ to $\begin{bmatrix}
      I & P
      \end{bmatrix}$ produces a matrix $P$ that satisfies $\left\lbrack \mathbf{x} \right\rbrack_{B} = P\left\lbrack \mathbf{x} \right\rbrack_{C}$ for all $\mathbf{x}$ in $V$.

